LOCAL CHANGES

    - Builds as Actually Portable Executable (APE) that runs natively on
      seven operating systems (Linux, macOS, Windows, FreeBSD, OpenBSD,
      NetBSD, bare metal) across two architectures (x86_64, aarch64)
      from a single binary
    - Links against Cosmopolitan libc instead of platform-native C libraries
    - Embeds Ruby standard library into /zip filesystem for single-file
      distribution (ruby.com contains everything needed to run)
    - Uses mimalloc as primary memory allocator instead of system malloc
    - YJIT currently only works on Linux (x86_64). The Rust JIT compiler
      is built targeting x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu which is not portable
      across the other platforms Cosmopolitan supports
